      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It’s a solid start and definitely sounds professional. I noticed it seems to be cutting off at the end though—it ends mid-sentence with \"through climate\". Could you finish that last paragraph and then expand the whole thing into a more detailed project summary? \n\nWe need to go into more detail about the actual implementation: the specific mangrove species we use, the community training programs, and how we monitor the impact over time. Just a reminder—the automated system is still looking for those specific pillars (resilience, biodiversity, stewardship, ecosystem, sustainability, mitigation, restoration), so make sure they are well-integrated, but please keep the writing natural and avoid making it feel like a list of buzzwords.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dear Grant Committee,\n\nAt GreenHorizon International, we are committed to preserving the delicate balance of coastal ecosystems, working tirelessly to establish a harmonious coexistence between human progress and environmental stewardship. Through our innovative and community-centered projects, we prioritize the restoration of vital mangrove forests, creating safe havens for local flora and fauna as they adapt to the dynamic challenges brought by changing sea levels. By fostering collaborative relationships with local communities, we empower them to play an active role in conservation efforts, ensuring sustainable practices that align with our mission to safeguard global biodiversity.\n\nOur twofold approach—both ecological and social—aims to prove that resilient coastal ecosystems are integral to environmental sustainability. We do not merely focus on individual species; instead, we elevate the well-being of entire ecosystems through proactive measures, scientific research, and a deep-rooted dedication to ecosystem stewardship. The unique combination of our community engagement and hands-on restoration projects positions us as a formidable contributor to the fight against biodiversity loss and a catalyst for positive environmental change.\n\nIn executing our mission, we implement several strategic initiatives designed to restore and maintain our coastal wetlands. We carefully select native mangrove species such as Avicennia germinans and Rhizophora mangle to cultivate in these habitats, providing",
